Description:
    Add React on Rails Pro to an existing React on Rails application.

Example:
    rails generate react_on_rails:pro

    This will add:
    - Pro initializer (config/initializers/react_on_rails_pro.rb)
    - Node renderer (renderer/node-renderer.js)
    - Node renderer process to Procfile.dev

Modifies:
    - package.json (replaces react-on-rails with react-on-rails-pro and
      react-on-rails-pro-node-renderer)

Bundler configuration:
    Upgrades serverWebpackConfig.js and ServerClientOrBoth.js in the active
    config/webpack/ or config/rspack/ directory only when both files exactly
    match a supported current generated pair. Enables Pro server settings,
    extractLoader, Babel SSR caller handling, and matching exports/imports.
    A supported pair using the legacy companion filename generateWebpackConfigs.js
    keeps that filename; it is not renamed.

    Customized, unknown, unsupported historical, incomplete, or ambiguous pairs
    are left unchanged, including their paths. If the pair is skipped, complete
    the manual migration before building and verifying SSR; rerunning the
    generator does not migrate these files:
    https://reactonrails.com/docs/pro/upgrading-to-pro/#complete-a-skipped-webpackrspack-migration-manually

Prerequisites:
    - React on Rails must be installed (rails g react_on_rails:install)
    - react_on_rails_pro gem must be in your Gemfile
